You are editing a NestJS + Next.js multi-tenant SaaS starter kit.

## Critical Rules
- All backend modules live in `apps/api/src/[feature]/`
- All frontend routes live in `apps/web/src/app/`
- Shared types live in `packages/shared/src/`
- Use `@shared/enums` for Permission, RoleName, PlanType, SubscriptionStatus
- Public endpoints require `@Public()` decorator (from `core/guards/jwt-auth.guard`)
- Protected endpoints require `@Permissions(...)` (from `core/guards/permission.guard`)
- Never use `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` — it's already global in AppModule
- All API returns use `ok()`/`fail()` from `@shared/response`
- Entities must have `organizationId` + `@Index()`
- Frontend uses `api.get/post/patch/del` from `lib/api-client.ts`
- UI authorization uses `<Can permission="...">` or `useAuthStore.hasPermission()`
- All responses follow envelope: `{ success, message, data, meta }`

## File Patterns
- Backend module: `controller.ts` + `service.ts` + `dto/*.ts` + `entities/*.ts` + `module.ts`
- Frontend feature: `app/dashboard/[feature]/page.tsx` + `components/[feature]-*.tsx`
- Migrations go in `apps/api/src/database/migrations/`

## Architecture
- Multi-tenant: every tenant-scoped entity has `organizationId`, all queries scoped by it
- Auth: JWT (HS256) with refresh token rotation; global guards in AppModule
- RBAC: 6 roles, enum-driven permissions, `PermissionGuard` resolves per-route
- Queue: BullMQ with Redis for async jobs (email, notifications, AI, cleanup)
- Response envelope: `{ success, message, data, meta }` via `ok()`/`fail()`

## Do Not
- Create new global modules
- Trust client-supplied IDs without scoping by `organizationId`
- Add `NEXT_PUBLIC_` to server-only env vars
- Change Sentry config filenames
- Skip TypeORM migrations when changing the schema

